{121}{See ya aroun'!}{See ya aroun'!}{}{}{}{}
{122}{e:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{123}{Let's see - On the east side of the island, there is the statue gardens at Norleigh Seahold, and Plainwicke Plantation has the oldest surviving windmill in all of Arcanum, if you're into such historical curiosities. They're both hundreds of years old. Ahh - There really isn't much more beyond that, I'm afraid.}{Let's see - On the east side of the island, there is the statue gardens at Norleigh Seahold, and Plainwicke Plantation has the oldest surviving windmill in all of Arcanum, if you're into such historical curiosities. They're both hundreds of years old. Ahh - There really isn't much more beyond that, I'm afraid.}{}{}{}{}
{124}{What about on the west side of the island?}{}{5}{}{128}{}
{125}{Oh, look at the time! I really must go now. Thanks for telling me this!}{}{5}{}{110}{}
{126}{Whut about the rest of da ile-lund?}{}{-4}{}{128}{}
{127}{Oh! Da time! Me must go now! Tanks for tell'n me dis!}{}{-4}{}{110}{}
{128}{I'm sorry, but all I know about the west side is there's a rich man's city they call Monaco. It's mostly humans. I never traveled that far while my parents were there and haven't seen a map in ages.}{I'm sorry, but all I know about the west side is there's a rich man's city they call Monaco. It's mostly humans. I never traveled that far while my parents were there and haven't seen a map in ages.}{}{}{}{}
{129}{Cattan sounds like a rather boring place, unless you're a scholar.}{}{5}{}{133}{}
{130}{Oh, look at the time! I really must go now. Thanks for telling me this!}{}{5}{}{110}{}
{131}{Cat-tan sounds boring - unless you be scholar.}{}{-4}{}{133}{}
{132}{Oh! Da time! Me must go now! Tanks for tell'n me dis!}{}{-4}{}{110}{}
{133}{I suppose it would be, for an adventurer. The island has been settled for a few thousand years, so most of the dangers were dealt with long ago. Cidua, who lives at the end of the main road, might be able to tell you more than I can.}{I suppose it would be, for an adventurer. The island has been settled for a few thousand years, so most of the dangers were dealt with long ago. Cidua, who lives at the end of the main road, might be able to tell you more than I can.}{}{}{}{}
